===Interjection===
{{en-intj}}

# {{ng|Expresses [[regret]], [[remorse]], or [[sorrow]].}}
#: {{syn|en|soz|q1=slang, chiefly Britain}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Sorry'''! I didn't see that you were on the phone.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Sorry''' about yesterday. — No worries.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Sorry''' I’m so late.}}
# {{ng|Said as a request to excuse one's unintentional behaviors.}}
#: {{syn|en|excuse me}}
#: {{ux|en|Oops! '''Sorry!'''}}
# {{ng|Said as a request to pass somebody.}}
#: {{syn|en|excuse me}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Sorry!''' Coming through!}}
# {{ng|Used as a request for someone to repeat something not heard or understood clearly.}}
#: {{syn|en|I beg your pardon?|I'm sorry?|say again|come again|excuse me?|q5=US|Thesaurus:say again}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Sorry'''? What was that? The phone cut out.}}
# {{ng|Used to correct oneself in speech.}}
#: {{ux|en|There are four—'''sorry''', ''five''—local branches of the store.}}
# {{ng|Used as a {{l|en|hedge|id=Q474726}}.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Sorry''', but I don't care what you think.}}

====Usage notes====
* The interjection is generally understood as a clipping of {{m|en|I'm sorry}}.
* A typically sarcastic use slows down the rhythm and stresses the final syllable, as {{IPAchar|/ˌsɒˈɹiːː/}}. This is often spelled as {{m|en|sorree}} or emphatically as something like ''sor-REE!!'' in print.

